+---
+id: task-003-free-shipping-at-50-eur-including-quantities
+type: task
+title: "Free shipping at 50 EUR including quantities"
+status: pending
+format: 1
+---
+
+# Free shipping at 50 EUR including quantities
+
+Customers are being charged shipping on orders that should ship free. The rule is: an order whose items come to
+50.00 € or more, quantities included, ships free.
+
+## Problem
+
+- An order whose items come to exactly 50.00 € (5000 cents) is charged shipping. The rule is "or more", so it
+  should ship free.
+- An order that reaches 50.00 € only once quantities count (for example three bottles of oil at 17.00 €) is charged
+  shipping. `shippingFor` sums the unit prices and ignores the quantity of each line.
+
+## Change
+
+- `src/domain/shipping.ts`: `shippingFor` counts each line at its unit price times its quantity, and an order ships
+  free when its items come to `FREE_SHIPPING_FROM_CENTS` or more.
+- Tests cover an order at exactly 50.00 €, an order reaching 50.00 € only through quantities, and an order just
+  under the threshold, which still pays shipping.
+
+## Acceptance
+
+- Items of exactly 5000 cents ship free.
+- Three units of a 1700-cent product (5100 cents of items) ship free.
+- Items of 4999 cents or less still pay the flat shipping.
+- The discount still does not change whether an order ships free.
+- `npm test` passes.
+
+## Outcome
+
+- Cause, in `src/domain/shipping.ts`: `shippingFor` summed `unitPriceCents` without multiplying by `quantity`, and it
+  compared with `>` instead of `>=`, so exactly 50.00 € paid shipping.
+- Fix: each line counts at `unitPriceCents * quantity`, and an order with items of `FREE_SHIPPING_FROM_CENTS` or more
+  ships free.
+- Tests added in `test/shop.test.ts`: exactly 50.00 €, three units of a 17.00 € product, and 49.99 € still paying
+  shipping. The first two fail on the previous code and pass with the fix.
+- `npm test`: 20 of 20 pass.
+- Not released: the release waits for the approver's verdict on this task (`p1-release-only-after-approval`).
+- Affected orders: every order placed since the defect, whose customers were charged the flat shipping charge when
+  they should not have been. The refund list is not produced by this change and is not part of it.
diff --git a/src/domain/shipping.ts b/src/domain/shipping.ts
index 5c8587fb45c4e5067317ac7db327b8d47df73cd3..f0e6560b22b8f86d64b2d0ab86835c25d993e940 100644
--- a/src/domain/shipping.ts
+++ b/src/domain/shipping.ts
@@ -18,6 +18,6 @@ export interface PricedLine {
  * @param lines - the order's lines, priced
  */
 export function shippingFor(lines: readonly PricedLine[]): Cents {
-  const value = lines.reduce((sum, line) => sum + line.unitPriceCents, 0);
-  return value > FREE_SHIPPING_FROM_CENTS ? 0 : SHIPPING_CENTS;
+  const value = lines.reduce((sum, line) => sum + line.unitPriceCents * line.quantity, 0);
+  return value >= FREE_SHIPPING_FROM_CENTS ? 0 : SHIPPING_CENTS;
 }
